<title>TAIWAN: TAIWAN TO LOWER FUEL PRICE 1-2 PCT ON JLY EARNINGS.</title>
<headline>TAIWAN TO LOWER FUEL PRICE 1-2 PCT ON JLY EARNINGS.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan state-run monopoly Chinese Petroleum Corp said on Friday it planned to cut its domestic fuel prices by one to two percent following sound profits in July.</p>
<p>Chinese Petroleum officials said the company would officially announce the price cuts later on Friday.</p>
</text>
